    "rationale": "Rule R02: prioritize earliest observed failure. The candidate's previous strategy emitted walk actions that required undirected edges, but the PDDL walk precondition is `(link ?start ?end)` and only the directed link facts exist; the nut locations (gate) are sinks, so the greedy algorithm got stuck after the first tighten. Rule R05: connect the diagnostic `executed_actions=7` (exactly one traversal of `shed->loc1->loc2->loc3->loc4`, pickup, `loc4->gate`, tighten) to the missing return path from gate, and verify the submitted source uses directed `out_link[f[1]].append(f[2])` rather than symmetric adjacency. Rule R08: keep the existing `get_plan` interface, deterministic spanner/nut/location ordering, and ≤1000-action cap; replace only the planning logic with a forward BFS over full frozenset states, parent-pointer reconstruction (the broken parent-pointer logic was the prior issue, so I include a careful reverse-walk here), and directed-link successors so that any sink-location plan (gate) requires carrying all spanners in a single trip -- which BFS finds automatically within depth 200.",
